        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Apple introduces the new 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 (137 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-introduces-the-new-14-inch-macbook-pro-with-m6/</link>
            <guid>50258521</guid>
            <pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:01:07 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-introduces-the-new-14-inch-macbook-pro-with-m6/">https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/apple-introduces-the-new-14-inch-macbook-pro-with-m6/</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50258521">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page">


	
    







 
<nav id="ac-localnav" lang="en-US" role="navigation" aria-label="Newsroom" data-analytics-region="local nav" data-sticky="">
	
    
    
        




    
    
    
	
	

</nav>





<main id="main" role="main"> 




<span id="opens-in-new-window">opens in new window</span>
<section>
<article data-analytics-activitymap-region-id="article">






    
    
    









    





    <div>
        
		
        <div>
                    
                    
                        <span>PRESS RELEASE</span>
                    
                    
                        <span>October 27, 2026</span>
                    
                    
                </div>

        <div>
                
                
                
                    <h2>
                        
    
        Apple introduces <br>the new 14‑inch&nbsp;<br>MacBook Pro with M6
    

                    </h2>
                
            </div>

        <div>
                
                
                    Supercharged by M6, the 14-inch MacBook Pro features incredible performance and next-level AI capabilities, enhanced connectivity, and up to 24 hours of battery life, delivering even more value
                
            </div>

        
            
    
    
    
    
    

        

    </div>







    
    
    






  
    
    
    
    
      <figure aria-label="Media, A side view of a partially open 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 is set against a glowing M6 logo in the background.">
        <div>
             
              
              <div>
                Supercharged by the all-new M6 chip, the 14-inch MacBook Pro brings extraordinary performance, AI capabilities, and up to 24 hours of battery life — making it an even more compelling value.
              </div>
            
            
            
            
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/10/apple-introduces-the-new-14-inch-macbook-pro-with-m6/article/Apple-MacBook-Pro-14-in-with-M6-hero-261027.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-MacBook-Pro-14-in-with-M6-hero-261027_big" aria-label="Download media, A side view of a partially open 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 is set against a glowing M6 logo in the background."></a>
          </div>
      </figure>
    
  








    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div><span>CUPERTINO, CALIFORNIA</span> Apple today announced the new <a href="https://www.apple.com/macbook-pro/" target="_blank">14-inch MacBook Pro with M6</a>, delivering even more performance, powerful on-device AI capabilities, and faster connectivity for college students, business users, creators, and more. M6 features an advanced 12-core CPU with the world’s fastest CPU core, so everything from productivity tasks to more demanding pro workflows feels incredibly fast and responsive.<sup>1</sup> The 12-core GPU delivers up to 30 percent faster graphics and up to 25 percent faster AI workloads when compared to M5, making the 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 a compelling value for users who need serious power.<sup>2</sup> For those upgrading from M1, the performance gains are even more significant, with up to 11x faster graphics and up to 13x faster AI performance.<sup>3</sup> With additional Neural Accelerators in the GPU and a Dual 16-core Neural Engine, M6 turns MacBook Pro into an even more powerful platform for AI — from taking advantage of Siri AI and Apple Intelligence features across apps and macOS to running LLMs locally, all while preserving user privacy.<sup>4</sup> In addition, the 14-inch MacBook Pro features Wi-Fi 7 and Bluetooth 6, while superfast storage makes working with large files, exporting projects, and running demanding AI workflows fly. And with phenomenal battery life of up to 24 hours, it delivers the same remarkable performance whether plugged in or on battery, so users can work, create, and pursue their passions from anywhere.<sup>3</sup> It also offers the advanced features users love, including the stunning Liquid Retina XDR display with a nano-texture option, a 12MP Center Stage camera, an immersive six-speaker sound system, and a wide array of ports. Together with macOS 27, the new 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 is a major upgrade for existing Mac users and those coming to Mac for the first time. Available in space black and silver, it can be pre-ordered beginning tomorrow, October 28, with availability starting Friday, November 6.
</div>
 

    
    
    






  
    
    
    
    
      <figure aria-label="Media, Two people perform fieldwork using MacBook Pro outdoors on a sunny day.">
        <div>
             
              
              <div>
                The new 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 combines next-generation performance and powerful on-device AI in a portable design, empowering students, creatives, developers, and business professionals to take their workflows anywhere.
              </div>
            
            
            
            
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/10/apple-introduces-the-new-14-inch-macbook-pro-with-m6/article/Apple-MacBook-Pro-14-in-with-M6-lifestyle-261027.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-MacBook-Pro-14-in-with-M6-lifestyle-261027_big" aria-label="Download media, Two people perform fieldwork using MacBook Pro outdoors on a sunny day."></a>
          </div>
      </figure>
    
  








    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>“The 14-inch MacBook Pro is the pro laptop of choice for a wide range of users — from college students, to business professionals across every industry, to multidisciplinary creators doing it all on one device,” said Shelly Goldberg, Apple’s vice president of Hardware Engineering. “With the powerful M6 chip, we’re taking performance to the next level, with a boost in CPU speed and graphics and even more powerful capabilities for on-device AI. With its amazing battery life, remarkable Liquid Retina XDR display, and even faster connectivity, the new 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 delivers a fantastic combination of performance, capability, and value.”
</div>
 

    
    
    






  
    
    
    
    
      <figure aria-label="Media, The Apple M6 logo.">
        <div>
             
              
              <div>
                M6 makes the 14-inch MacBook Pro faster than ever, thanks to a powerful 12-core CPU, advanced 12-core GPU, and Dual 16-core Neural Engine.
              </div>
            
            
            
            
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/images/2026/10/apple-introduces-the-new-14-inch-macbook-pro-with-m6/article/Apple-MacBook-Pro-14-in-with-M6-chip-261027.zip" download="" data-analytics-title="download image - Apple-MacBook-Pro-14-in-with-M6-chip-261027_big" aria-label="Download media, The Apple M6 logo."></a>
          </div>
      </figure>
    
  








    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <h2><strong>M6: Blazing-Fast Performance and On-Device AI Capabilities</strong>
</h2>
                 
             
                 <div>M6 brings even more performance and next-level AI capabilities to the 14-inch MacBook Pro. Featuring a powerful 12-core CPU, a 12-core GPU with Neural Accelerators in each core, Dual 16-core Neural Engine, and faster unified memory, MacBook Pro with M6 is faster and more responsive.
</div>
                 
             
                 <div>The 12-core CPU, with two more cores than before, brings blazing-fast single- and multithreaded performance, so users can fly through everything from multitasking across apps to compiling code to handling complex creative workflows. The 12-core GPU, also with two additional cores, delivers up to 30 percent faster graphics performance when compared to M5.<sup>2</sup> Everything from 3D modeling to photo editing and gaming feels incredibly fast, enhanced by a third-generation ray-tracing engine and Dynamic Caching to optimize on-chip memory. It also brings up to 25 percent faster performance for on-device AI workloads, like LLM prompt processing, compared to M5.<sup>3</sup> The Dual 16-core Neural Engine delivers up to 1.9x faster performance than M5 and works with the advanced GPU to dramatically accelerate AI workloads like image generation, Super Resolution, and AI upscaling.<sup>2</sup> The Neural Engine also powers Apple Intelligence, enabling advanced and energy-efficient on-device AI processing. The 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 does all this with industry-leading performance per watt and up to 24 hours of battery life, the longest ever in a Mac. With 16GB of unified memory standard, configurable up to 32GB, and higher memory bandwidth up to 170GB/s, MacBook Pro makes multitasking and working with demanding apps and large projects even faster.
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    


    
    <div data-component-list="ScrollAnimationDefault AutoPlayVideo">The 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6 helps motion designers model 3D objects, design product visualizations, and render animations with ease.</div>






    
    
    


     
     
    
    
        <div>
             
                 <div><strong>The 14-inch MacBook Pro with M6&nbsp;enables</strong>:<sup>3</sup>
</div>
                 
             
                 <div><ul>
<li>Up to 13x faster time to first token performance for LLM prompt processing compared to the 13-inch MacBook Pro with M1, and up to 1.3x faster than the 14-inch MacBook Pro with M5.</li>
</ul>
</div>
                 
             
                 <div><ul>
<li>Up to 11.7x faster render performance with ray tracing in Blender compared to the 13-inch MacBook Pro with M1, and up to 1.3x faster than the 14-inch MacBook Pro with M5.</li>
</ul>
</div>
                 
             
                 <div><ul>
<li>Up to 3.3x faster image-processing performance in Affinity compared to the 13-inch MacBook Pro with M1, and up to 1.2x faster than the 14-inch MacBook Pro with M5.</li>
</ul>
</div>
                 
             
                 <div><ul>
<li>Up to 2.5x faster project build performance when compiling code in Xcode compared to the 13-inch MacBook Pro with M1, and up to 1.3x faster than the 14-inch MacBook Pro with M5.</li>
</ul>
</div>
                 
             
         </div>
 

    
    
    


    
    
        
        
        
