  mixed-precision division <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Deferred-Words.html#index-IS-_0028-xt-_002e_002e_002e-_0022name_0022-_002d_002d-_0029-core_002dext">is</a> now faster
  support <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Counted-Loops.html#index-FOR-_0028-compilation-_002d_002d-do_002dsys-_003b-run_002dtime-u-_002d_002d-loop_002dsys-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">for</a> int128 types <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Boolean-Flags.html#index-on-_0028-a_002daddr-_002d_002d-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">on</a> AMD64
  workarounds <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Counted-Loops.html#index-FOR-_0028-compilation-_002d_002d-do_002dsys-_003b-run_002dtime-u-_002d_002d-loop_002dsys-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">for</a> gcc performance bugs (in particular, PR 15242)
  branch target alignment (good speedup <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Boolean-Flags.html#index-on-_0028-a_002daddr-_002d_002d-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">on</a> Alpha).</code></pre>
<h2 id="user-visible-changes-between-061-and-062">User-visible changes
between 0.6.1 and 0.6.2:</h2>
<pre><code>Bug fixes (in particular, gforth-0.6.2 compiles with gcc-3.3)
<a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Basic-Mini_002dOOF-Usage.html#index-new-_0028-class-_002d_002d-o-_0029-mini_002doof">New</a> words: LATEST, <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Anonymous-Definitions.html#index-latestxt-_0028-_002d_002d-xt-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e6">LATESTXT</a> (LASTXT deprecated)
Operating environment: Added optional support <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Counted-Loops.html#index-FOR-_0028-compilation-_002d_002d-do_002dsys-_003b-run_002dtime-u-_002d_002d-loop_002dsys-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">for</a> a C <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Objects-Glossary.html#index-interface-_0028-_002d_002d-_0029-objects">interface</a> built
  <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Boolean-Flags.html#index-on-_0028-a_002daddr-_002d_002d-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">on</a> the ffcall libraries (more portable <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Bitwise-operations.html#index-and-_0028-w1-w2-_002d_002d-w-_0029-core">and</a> powerful than the old
  one, but still not documented).  <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Values.html#index-TO-_0028-value-_002e_002e_002e-_0022name_0022-_002d_002d-_0029-core_002dext">To</a> <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Blocks.html#index-use-_0028-_0022file_0022-_002d_002d-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">use</a> it, the ffcall libraries
  have <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Values.html#index-TO-_0028-value-_002e_002e_002e-_0022name_0022-_002d_002d-_0029-core_002dext">to</a> be installed before building <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Environmental-Queries.html#index-gforth-_0028-_002d_002d-c_002daddr-u-_0029-gforth_002denvironment">Gforth</a> (see INSTALL).
Miscellaneous: Gforth-fast now uses <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Class-Declaration.html#index-static-_0028-_002d_002d-_0029-oof">static</a> superinstructions (some
  speedup <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Boolean-Flags.html#index-on-_0028-a_002daddr-_002d_002d-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">on</a> some platforms); generally <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Objects-Glossary.html#index-this-_0028-_002d_002d-object-_0029-objects">this</a> <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Deferred-Words.html#index-IS-_0028-xt-_002e_002e_002e-_0022name_0022-_002d_002d-_0029-core_002dext">is</a> transparent (apart
  from the speedup), but there are lots <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/General-control-structures-with-CASE.html#index-of-_0028-compilation-_002d_002d-of_002dsys-_003b-run_002dtime-x1-x2-_002d_002d-_007cx1-_0029-core_002dext">of</a> command-line options <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Counted-Loops.html#index-FOR-_0028-compilation-_002d_002d-do_002dsys-_003b-run_002dtime-u-_002d_002d-loop_002dsys-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">for</a>
  controlling the <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Class-Declaration.html#index-static-_0028-_002d_002d-_0029-oof">static</a> superinstruction generation.</code></pre>
<h2 id="user-visible-changes-between-060-and-061">User-visible changes
between 0.6.0 and 0.6.1:</h2>
<pre><code>Bug fixes (installation <a href="https://gforth.org/manual/1.0/Boolean-Flags.html#index-on-_0028-a_002daddr-_002d_002d-_0029-gforth_002d0_002e2">on</a> big-endian machines sometimes did not work)</code></pre>
